"paint_probe.mst — drawing through the WM_PAINT HDC (DolphinDart DD9).

 The door has delivered the HDC since DD7; nothing had yet DRAWN with it. This
 is the smallest thing that proves the whole chain — real WM_PAINT -> door ->
 UiSession -> a Smalltalk handler -> a GDI call through the generated prims —
 and it proves it by READING THE RESULT BACK, not by counting that the handler
 ran.

 A paint count only says a handler was entered. `SetPixelV` followed by
 `GetPixel` at the same coordinate says the device context we were handed is a
 real one, that the call reached GDI with the right argument order, and that
 the pixel landed where we asked. If any link is broken the readback answers
 CLR_INVALID (16rFFFFFFFF) or the wrong colour — it cannot answer the value we
 wrote by accident."
UiWindow subclass: PaintProbe [
    | probed readback textOk |

    "COLORREF is 0x00BBGGRR, so this is pure blue — deliberately not the window
     background, not black and not white, so a matching readback cannot be
     matching something that was already there."
    PaintProbe class >> inkColor [ ^16rFF0000 ]
    PaintProbe class >> inkX [ ^12 ]
    PaintProbe class >> inkY [ ^9 ]

    initWindow [ super initWindow. probed := 0. readback := nil. textOk := false ]
    probed [ ^probed ]
    readback [ ^readback ]
    textOk [ ^textOk ]

    onPaint: hdc [
        | s |
        super onPaint: hdc.
        probed := probed + 1.
        Gdi32
            setPixelV: hdc
            x: PaintProbe inkX
            y: PaintProbe inkY
            crColor: PaintProbe inkColor.
        "Read it straight back, inside the same BeginPaint/EndPaint pair — the
         HDC is only valid here, and reading later would test a different DC."
        readback := Gdi32
            getPixel: hdc
            xPos: PaintProbe inkX
            yPos: PaintProbe inkY.
        "And some text, which is what the gate's snapshot will show.

         The STRING goes in, not its address: the generated wrapper marshals it
         (`FFICoerce stringTemp:` -> a Utf16Buffer freed under `ensure:`), and
         handing it a raw address instead is refused outright — 'FFI: cannot
         pass SmallInteger as a string argument'. That refusal is the floor
         working as designed; a wrapper that accepted an integer here would
         hand TextOutW whatever happened to be at that address.

         `cbString` is a CHARACTER count, not a byte count. The two differ by a
         factor of two for UTF-16, and passing bytes draws trailing garbage
         from past the end of the string."
        s := 'DolphinDart'.
        textOk := (Gdi32
            textOut: hdc
            nXStart: 20
            nYStart: 24
            lpString: s
            cbString: s size) ~= 0.
        ^0
    ]
]
